{"id": "tea:yoginihrdaya:1.1", "source": "src:yoginihrdaya", "location": {"ref": "1.1"}, "paraphrase": "The Goddess asks Bhairava: in the Vāmakeśvara Tantra there are many matters whose meaning is not known; explain them all.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission"], "speaker": "the Goddess", "addressee": "Bhairava", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yoginihrdaya:1.13", "source": "src:yoginihrdaya", "location": {"ref": "1.13"}, "paraphrase": "This cakra is ninefold and has nine distinct mantras.", "tags": {"level": "unmarked", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["ritual"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice"], "concepts": ["cpt:nine-avaranas"], "speaker": "Bhairava (Śiva)", "addressee": "the Goddess", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yoginihrdaya:1.2", "source": "src:yoginihrdaya", "location": {"ref": "1.2"}, "paraphrase": "Bhairava: hear, O Goddess, the great secret, the supreme Yoginīhṛdaya; out of love for you I tell it today; it must be guarded with special care.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission"], "concepts": ["cpt:srividya-secrecy"], "speaker": "Bhairava (Śiva)", "addressee": "the Goddess", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yoginihrdaya:1.41-42", "source": "src:yoginihrdaya", "location": {"ref": "1.41-42"}, "paraphrase": "The four powers, fused in pairs, became the four seats Kāmarūpa, Pūrṇagiri, Jālandhara and Oḍḍiyāna; the seats stand in order in the bulb (kanda), in pada, in rūpa and beyond form (rūpātīta).", "tags": {"level": "unmarked", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["body-layers"], "concepts": ["cpt:four-pithas-srividya"], "terms": ["trm:pitha", "trm:kamarupa", "trm:oddiyana", "trm:jalandhara", "trm:purnagiri"], "notes": "1.41 as read with the Dīpikā, which glosses the four syllables as the four pīṭhas; 1.42 root checked.", "speaker": "Bhairava (Śiva)", "addressee": "the Goddess", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yoginihrdaya:1.6", "source": "src:yoginihrdaya", "location": {"ref": "1.6"}, "paraphrase": "The code (saṅketa) of the goddess Tripurā is threefold: the code of the cakra, the code of the mantra and the code of worship.", "tags": {"level": "unmarked", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["ritual", "sound", "knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice", "teacher-transmission"], "original": {"text": "cakrasaṅketako mantrapūjāsaṅketakau tathā / trividhas tripurādevyāḥ saṅketaḥ parameśvari", "script": "IAST", "edition": "Benares 1923 ed. with Dīpikā (Muktabodha M00115)", "licence": "public-domain text; short quotation"}, "concepts": ["cpt:three-sanketas"], "terms": ["trm:sanketa", "trm:tripura"], "speaker": "Bhairava (Śiva)", "addressee": "the Goddess", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yoginihrdaya:1.86", "source": "src:yoginihrdaya", "location": {"ref": "1.86"}, "paraphrase": "Thus the code of the great cakra of Tripurā has been told, O supreme Goddess, which brings about liberation while living.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "ritual"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["karma-liberation"], "concepts": ["cpt:jivanmukti", "cpt:three-sanketas"], "speaker": "Bhairava (Śiva)", "addressee": "the Goddess", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yoginihrdaya:1.9-10", "source": "src:yoginihrdaya", "location": {"ref": "1.9-10"}, "paraphrase": "When the supreme Śakti, of her own will taking the form of the universe, beholds her own vibrancy (sphurattā), then the cakra comes into being.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "cosmic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["world-fate", "ultimate"], "original": {"text": "yadā sā paramā śaktiḥ svecchayā viśvarūpiṇī / sphurattām ātmanaḥ paśyet tadā cakrasya sambhavaḥ", "script": "IAST", "edition": "Benares 1923 ed. with Dīpikā (Muktabodha M00115)", "licence": "public-domain text; short quotation"}, "concepts": ["cpt:sri-yantra", "cpt:siva-sakti-union", "cpt:prakasa-vimarsa"], "disputes": ["dsp:causation"], "speaker": "Bhairava (Śiva)", "addressee": "the Goddess", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yoginihrdaya:2.15-16", "source": "src:yoginihrdaya", "location": {"ref": "2.15-16"}, "paraphrase": "The mantra-code is sixfold: the literal meaning (bhāvārtha), the traditional meaning (sampradāyārtha), the hidden meaning (nigarbhārtha), the Kaula meaning (kaulikārtha), the all-secret meaning (sarvarahasyārtha) and the meaning of the great principle (mahātattvārtha); the literal meaning is simply the sense of the syllables.", "tags": {"level": "unmarked", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["sound", "knowledge"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["sound-language"], "original": {"text": "bhāvārthaḥ sampradāyārtho nigarbhārthaś ca kaulikaḥ / tathā sarvarahasyārtho mahātattvārtha eva ca", "script": "IAST", "edition": "Benares 1923 ed. with Dīpikā (Muktabodha M00115)", "licence": "public-domain text; short quotation"}, "concepts": ["cpt:six-meanings-of-mantra"], "terms": ["trm:sadvidhartha"], "speaker": "Bhairava (Śiva)", "addressee": "the Goddess", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yoginihrdaya:2.48", "source": "src:yoginihrdaya", "location": {"ref": "2.48"}, "paraphrase": "The hidden meaning (nigarbha) has as its domain Śiva, the guru and the self.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["sound-language", "teacher-transmission"], "concepts": ["cpt:six-meanings-of-mantra"], "speaker": "Bhairava (Śiva)", "addressee": "the Goddess", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yoginihrdaya:2.51-52", "source": "src:yoginihrdaya", "location": {"ref": "2.51-52"}, "paraphrase": "The Kaula meaning is the oneness of the cakra and the deity, and of the vidyā, the guru and the self.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "ritual"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["sound-language", "ultimate"], "concepts": ["cpt:six-meanings-of-mantra", "cpt:unity-of-guru-mantra-deity-self"], "speaker": "Bhairava (Śiva)", "addressee": "the Goddess", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yoginihrdaya:2.73-74", "source": "src:yoginihrdaya", "location": {"ref": "2.73-74"}, "paraphrase": "The meaning of the great principle: in the partless, supreme, subtle, unmarkable principle, free of all states, beyond space, whose body is light and bliss, transcending and pervading the universe — (the self is to be dissolved there).", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "apophatic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ultimate"], "concepts": ["cpt:six-meanings-of-mantra", "cpt:lalita-as-brahman"], "notes": "Only the opening of the passage checked; the closing clause is summarized from the Dīpikā's gloss.", "speaker": "Bhairava (Śiva)", "addressee": "the Goddess", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yoginihrdaya:2.81", "source": "src:yoginihrdaya", "location": {"ref": "2.81"}, "paraphrase": "Those who lack the succession of teachers and are proud of mere knowledge — through their breach of the samaya the rays (marīci) turn against them.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission", "powers-experiences"], "original": {"text": "pāramparyavihīnā ye jñānamātreṇa garvitāḥ / teṣāṃ samayalopena vikurvanti marīcayaḥ", "script": "IAST", "edition": "Benares 1923 ed. with Dīpikā (Muktabodha M00115)", "licence": "public-domain text; short quotation"}, "obstacles": ["obs:paramparya-hina-jnana", "obs:samaya-lopa"], "concepts": ["cpt:srividya-secrecy"], "speaker": "Bhairava (Śiva)", "addressee": "the Goddess", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yoginihrdaya:2.85", "source": "src:yoginihrdaya", "location": {"ref": "2.85"}, "paraphrase": "Thus this supreme knowledge, the domain of the letters of the vidyā and the āgamas, secret and sixfold, hard to penetrate, has been explained; by awakening to it one at once becomes lord of the circle of heroes.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["sound", "knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["sound-language", "karma-liberation"], "concepts": ["cpt:six-meanings-of-mantra"], "notes": "Wording as in the Setubandha text (paṭala 7 end).", "speaker": "Bhairava (Śiva)", "addressee": "the Goddess", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yoginihrdaya:3.1", "source": "src:yoginihrdaya", "location": {"ref": "3.1"}, "paraphrase": "Now I shall tell the code of worship, by merely awakening to which one rejoices, liberated while living.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["ritual", "knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice", "karma-liberation"], "concepts": ["cpt:three-pujas"], "speaker": "Bhairava (Śiva)", "addressee": "the Goddess", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yoginihrdaya:3.2-3", "source": "src:yoginihrdaya", "location": {"ref": "3.2-3"}, "paraphrase": "Your worship, ever arisen, is of three kinds: the supreme (parā), the non-supreme (aparā) and the supreme-non-supreme (parāparā). The first abides in non-duality and ranges over every outflow of the senses; the second, the worship of the cakra, is always performed by me.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["ritual", "meditation", "knowledge"], "stage": "all", "stage_native": "aparā - parāparā - parā pūjā"}, "types": ["practice"], "concepts": ["cpt:three-pujas"], "paths": ["pth:yoginihrdaya-three-pujas"], "practices": ["prc:sricakra-navavarana-puja"], "disputes": ["dsp:external-or-internal-worship"], "speaker": "Bhairava (Śiva)", "addressee": "the Goddess", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
